{"archetypes":[{"name":"oos-flow","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes OOS_PENDING gating across Step 2, ship-pr, Python ship, checkpoint, sentinels, and larch-log evidence where ordering mistakes can deadlock or bypass filing.","prompt_body":"Investigate the end-to-end OOS disposition state machine across step2-implement.sh, ship-pr.sh, python/ship.py, oos-disposition-checkpoint.sh, and the new oos-pipeline.md contract. Focus on whether manifest materialization, OOS_PENDING transitions, sentinel recovery, design-export resolution, security-routed observations, and PR creation gating happen in the intended order without creating infinite stalls or false clears. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bash-materializer","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The new materialize-manifest-oos.sh performs nontrivial jq extraction, sanitization, idempotency, security routing, and monotonic heading allocation in Bash.","prompt_body":"Review the Bash implementation of materialize-manifest-oos.sh and its call sites for shell correctness, error handling, idempotency, quoting, jq behavior, and portability under set -euo pipefail. Pay special attention to title normalization, duplicate detection, security focus-area predicates, redaction pipelines, multiline descriptions, and whether failure semantics match the documented caller behavior. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"python-ship","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The Python ship path now mirrors Bash OOS handling and may diverge in path resolution, state writes, disposition checks, or test expectations.","prompt_body":"Audit the Python OOS shipping path in python/ship.py, python/oos.py, and related tests for parity with the Bash workflow. Check whether accepted-file detection, design path resolution, oos-issues.ndjson discovery, manifest materialization, ctx.oos_pending handling, and disposition_ok inputs permit PR creation only after valid disposition evidence. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"redaction-boundary","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Manifest OOS data is transformed into public filing surfaces while security-routed observations are retained privately, making boundary and redaction mistakes high impact.","prompt_body":"Examine how manifest OOS titles, descriptions, focus areas, logs, sentinels, and execution-issue breadcrumbs move between public issue-filing surfaces and private security disposition surfaces. Verify that secrets, internal URLs, PII, and security-routed details are not exposed through oos-accepted-main-agent.md, oos-issues logs, failure logs, PR bodies, or test fixtures beyond intended sanitized forms. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"contract-sync","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"This change relies on synchronized normative docs, SKILL.md directives, structure tests, Makefile targets, and helper contracts to keep future orchestrator behavior coherent.","prompt_body":"Review whether the new and updated contracts stay internally consistent across SKILL.md, oos-pipeline.md, materialize-manifest-oos.md, SECURITY.md, Makefile wiring, and structure tests. Look for stale references, contradictory ownership of run-statistics versus oos-issues evidence, missing load directives, mismatched sentinel formats, or assertions that prove weaker behavior than the contract claims. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
